Instead of the preamble you can append runfiles.bat to your script at build time and call the labels directly. The script must exit /b before the end so execution does not run into the appended library. genrule( name = "my_tool_bundled", srcs = ["my_tool_body.bat", "@rules_batch//batch/runfiles:runfiles.bat"], outs = ["my_tool_bundled.bat"], cmd = "cat $(SRCS) > $@",
) call :rlocation "my_module/data/config.txt" CONFIG_PATH
call :runfiles_export_envvars Both calls run in their own scope and only write their results to your environment, plus a few _rl_RM_* cache variables.

